00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:49,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ]

1
00:00:50,154 --> 00:00:53,324
THE ORDINARY JACKPOT

2
00:01:05,753 --> 00:01:08,589
<i>Sometimes, I get so caught up working</i>

3
00:01:08,673 --> 00:01:10,758
<i>and end up alone in the office.</i>

4
00:01:12,468 --> 00:01:13,886
<i>When that happens</i>

5
00:01:13,969 --> 00:01:16,389
<i>part of me wants to leave</i>
<i>as soon as I can</i>

6
00:01:17,890 --> 00:01:19,684
<i>while another part of me</i>

7
00:01:20,351 --> 00:01:21,769
<i>feels proud of working hard.</i>

8
00:01:23,229 --> 00:01:26,357
<i>I even fool myself into thinking</i>

9
00:01:26,440 --> 00:01:28,109
<i>I'm the most important person</i>
<i>in the company.</i>

10
00:01:31,696 --> 00:01:34,156
<i>I have 1.3 billion won.</i>

11
00:01:35,199 --> 00:01:39,161
<i>But that's not enough to quit my job</i>
<i>or completely change my life.</i>

12
00:01:41,080 --> 00:01:44,875
<i>I can't decide what to do</i>
<i>with the money.</i>

13
00:01:45,334 --> 00:01:48,045
<i>So I continue going to work.</i>

14
00:01:56,095 --> 00:01:59,849
<i>In the meantime,</i>
<i>while I'm stuck in indecision...</i>

15
00:02:01,851 --> 00:02:05,604
<i>someone else is taking</i>
<i>the biggest leap of their life.</i>

16
00:02:31,464 --> 00:02:33,549
RESIGNATION LETTER
JEONG SEON-HYUK

17
00:02:34,675 --> 00:02:38,429
If you want a raise or more benefits,
or if the work is too tough

18
00:02:39,096 --> 00:02:41,515
just say so
instead of pulling a stunt like this.

19
00:02:42,975 --> 00:02:45,728
It's not that.
I'm really planning to leave.

20
00:02:47,021 --> 00:02:49,523
Isn't your kid starting school soon?
Can you afford to quit?

21
00:02:49,982 --> 00:02:52,443
Yes, we'll be fine for now.

22
00:02:54,528 --> 00:02:56,405
What brought this on all of a sudden?

23
00:02:56,739 --> 00:02:59,366
Honestly, didn't you
see this coming, Ms. Park?

24
00:02:59,909 --> 00:03:01,160
If I try to make a move

25
00:03:01,243 --> 00:03:04,121
it feels like I'm getting in the way
of the others' promotions.

26
00:03:04,747 --> 00:03:06,457
But if I do nothing

27
00:03:06,540 --> 00:03:09,168
it feels like I'm holding back
the newer, younger employees.

28
00:03:10,878 --> 00:03:13,088
Mr. Jeong, you are so...

29
00:03:13,172 --> 00:03:14,340
Pathetic, aren't I?

30
00:03:14,590 --> 00:03:15,800
Trust me, I know.

31
00:03:16,383 --> 00:03:17,510
I know that

32
00:03:18,344 --> 00:03:20,846
but once I took a passive approach

33
00:03:20,930 --> 00:03:23,182
it was hard to break out of it.

34
00:03:23,974 --> 00:03:27,102
So I'm trying to change
my environment instead.

35
00:03:29,188 --> 00:03:30,231
Starting your own business?

36
00:03:34,193 --> 00:03:36,779
I won't make you sign
a non-compete agreement

37
00:03:37,196 --> 00:03:38,280
so be honest with me.

38
00:03:49,917 --> 00:03:56,173
EPISODE 4:
MUTUAL CAUSE, MUTUAL EFFECT

39
00:03:58,843 --> 00:04:00,678
- Hello, Ju-hui.
- Hello.

40
00:04:01,971 --> 00:04:03,597
Come on, get to work on time.

41
00:04:03,681 --> 00:04:04,807
A team leader shouldn't be last.

42
00:04:05,558 --> 00:04:07,184
Right, my apologies.

43
00:04:07,268 --> 00:04:09,144
You've been
exactly 13 minutes late lately.

44
00:04:09,228 --> 00:04:10,229
Going to the gym?

45
00:04:10,563 --> 00:04:12,189
I had something to take care of.

46
00:04:15,234 --> 00:04:16,527
We all have our own things going on.

47
00:04:17,486 --> 00:04:20,281
That's an excuse for a rookie,
not a team leader.

48
00:04:22,366 --> 00:04:23,367
I'm sorry.

49
00:04:28,956 --> 00:04:30,207
And where's Mr. Jeong?

50
00:04:31,250 --> 00:04:33,544
Even if he's quitting,
he should still get here on time.

51
00:04:34,211 --> 00:04:35,504
Isn't that common courtesy?

52
00:04:35,588 --> 00:04:37,590
He said he was going
to stop by the mall today

53
00:04:37,673 --> 00:04:39,383
to say his goodbyes.

54
00:04:40,885 --> 00:04:43,178
Everyone's just doing
whatever they want.

55
00:04:43,846 --> 00:04:45,764
Is this a playground?
A train station?

56
00:04:48,934 --> 00:04:50,561
How ridiculous.

57
00:04:56,483 --> 00:04:58,110
All right, let's start the meeting.

58
00:04:58,193 --> 00:04:59,445
We have a lot to go over.

59
00:05:01,530 --> 00:05:02,990
Gi-tae, when are you going
to the mall?

60
00:05:03,073 --> 00:05:04,533
I'll head over right after lunch.

61
00:05:04,617 --> 00:05:06,619
They need to finish construction
this week

62
00:05:06,702 --> 00:05:08,370
so keep morale up,
but keep the pressure on too.

63
00:05:08,454 --> 00:05:09,455
Got it.

64
00:05:09,538 --> 00:05:11,874
Also, tonight at 8 p.m.

65
00:05:12,416 --> 00:05:13,417
You remember, correct?

66
00:05:13,709 --> 00:05:14,710
Yes.

67
00:05:17,796 --> 00:05:19,298
6TH FLOOR SALES DIVISION 1

68
00:05:23,719 --> 00:05:27,181
Assistant Manager Jang Hyang-eun
will join our team next week.

69
00:05:28,182 --> 00:05:29,183
But she's already here.

70
00:05:29,600 --> 00:05:30,601
Pardon?

71
00:05:31,977 --> 00:05:32,978
Hello, Mr. Gong.

72
00:05:35,022 --> 00:05:36,815
Oh, hello, Ms. Jang.

73
00:05:37,816 --> 00:05:39,443
What brings you here?

74
00:05:39,526 --> 00:05:42,488
I came to say hello
and meet our business partners.

75
00:05:42,905 --> 00:05:44,198
Have you been well?

76
00:05:44,281 --> 00:05:45,616
Yes, it's been a long time.

77
00:05:45,866 --> 00:05:46,867
Right.

78
00:05:47,534 --> 00:05:48,535
Hello, Mr. Yang.

79
00:05:48,786 --> 00:05:51,288
Wow, long time no see.
I look forward to working with you.

80
00:05:51,956 --> 00:05:53,165
Likewise.

81
00:05:53,248 --> 00:05:55,417
You haven't met these two yet,
have you?

82
00:05:55,501 --> 00:05:57,336
- This is...
- Gi-tae?

83
00:05:57,419 --> 00:05:58,545
Hello, ma'am.

84
00:05:59,088 --> 00:06:00,130
I've heard a lot about you.

85
00:06:00,673 --> 00:06:02,174
All good things, I hope.

86
00:06:02,758 --> 00:06:03,884
Yes, of course.

87
00:06:05,052 --> 00:06:06,053
And you're Ji-hye?

88
00:06:06,136 --> 00:06:08,097
I look forward
to working with you, ma'am.

89
00:06:08,347 --> 00:06:10,849
- Are you managing the center?
- Yes.

90
00:06:10,933 --> 00:06:12,434
Can I ask you a favor?

91
00:06:12,518 --> 00:06:13,978
Of course, anything.

92
00:06:14,061 --> 00:06:16,438
I'd like the following information
by my first official day.

93
00:06:16,522 --> 00:06:19,149
Baseline margins for the brands
Team 5 is in charge of.

94
00:06:19,233 --> 00:06:20,442
Customer prices.

95
00:06:20,526 --> 00:06:22,152
Each brand's customer service manual.

96
00:06:22,236 --> 00:06:23,445
Credit memo logs.

97
00:06:23,529 --> 00:06:24,697
Invoice checklists.

98
00:06:24,780 --> 00:06:26,365
Total penalty points.

99
00:06:26,448 --> 00:06:29,159
Direct numbers for all brand reps
as well as their email addresses.

100
00:06:29,618 --> 00:06:31,453
Can you put that together for me?

101
00:06:34,498 --> 00:06:37,209
Baseline margins, customer prices...

102
00:06:37,459 --> 00:06:38,669
Customer service manuals.

103
00:06:38,752 --> 00:06:40,254
I'd be disappointed
if I had to repeat myself.

104
00:06:42,715 --> 00:06:44,675
I'll say hello to Ms. Park.

105
00:06:50,389 --> 00:06:51,390
That's Ms. Jang.

106
00:06:52,349 --> 00:06:53,767
She was always good at her job, no?

107
00:06:54,101 --> 00:06:55,394
She hasn't changed a bit.

108
00:06:55,936 --> 00:06:56,937
Is this right?

109
00:06:57,021 --> 00:06:58,480
Will Ji-hye and I be okay?

110
00:06:59,064 --> 00:07:00,524
Of course not.

111
00:07:00,607 --> 00:07:01,900
You're screwed.

112
00:07:01,984 --> 00:07:03,193
DAILY ROUTINE

113
00:07:03,277 --> 00:07:04,361
<i>Thank you.</i>

114
00:07:08,490 --> 00:07:10,743
I didn't know there was
a spot like this nearby.

115
00:07:10,826 --> 00:07:12,578
Most of our colleagues don't know.

116
00:07:12,661 --> 00:07:14,705
I stop by every morning before work.

117
00:07:15,247 --> 00:07:18,125
So you called me to ask
about Jang Hyang-eun, right?

118
00:07:18,542 --> 00:07:21,295
Yeah, she's joining my team,
so I need to know more about her.

119
00:07:21,378 --> 00:07:23,255
I told you all I know last time.

120
00:07:23,338 --> 00:07:25,382
Something happened
while she was at the China branch.

121
00:07:25,466 --> 00:07:28,469
But they kept a tight lid on it,
so no one knows the details.

122
00:07:29,178 --> 00:07:32,806
They froze all personnel transfers,
but she managed to return to Korea.

123
00:07:33,474 --> 00:07:34,475
That's everything.

124
00:07:34,683 --> 00:07:36,685
So you don't actually know anything.

125
00:07:37,102 --> 00:07:38,145
I don't.

126
00:07:38,937 --> 00:07:40,856
But nothing good will come
from getting involved with her.

127
00:07:40,939 --> 00:07:42,524
Whatever she did while she was there

128
00:07:42,608 --> 00:07:44,943
it'll only make it harder
to work with the China branch.

129
00:07:45,694 --> 00:07:46,904
All right, then.

130
00:07:46,987 --> 00:07:48,572
I'm sure she'll tell me
when she's ready.

131
00:07:49,531 --> 00:07:51,742
That's a good mindset.
Just take it easy.

132
00:07:52,242 --> 00:07:54,995
All you need to think about is
how to utilize your team members.

133
00:07:55,496 --> 00:07:57,414
Ms. Jang should take over
the center now.

134
00:07:58,916 --> 00:08:01,627
I said, think about it.
Really think it through.

135
00:08:05,380 --> 00:08:06,924
What about Lee Ji-hye?

136
00:08:07,299 --> 00:08:09,301
She's only a contract worker,
so she must be anxious already.

137
00:08:09,384 --> 00:08:12,012
And now this woman flies in
from China and takes her spot?

138
00:08:12,096 --> 00:08:13,639
How do you think she'd feel?

139
00:08:15,933 --> 00:08:17,351
Even so, work is work.

140
00:08:19,228 --> 00:08:21,146
You're so cold-blooded.

141
00:08:21,814 --> 00:08:23,899
Don't you have any empathy?

142
00:08:25,818 --> 00:08:27,069
What about you?

143
00:08:27,152 --> 00:08:29,446
You claim to be such an empath.

144
00:08:29,822 --> 00:08:31,740
But why don't you empathize with me?

145
00:08:32,366 --> 00:08:34,159
You sure have a way with words.

146
00:08:35,202 --> 00:08:38,288
Anyway, keep doing your job

147
00:08:38,997 --> 00:08:41,875
but don't forget to look out
for your team, Mr. Gong.

148
00:08:43,418 --> 00:08:44,711
I got this for you.

149
00:08:45,212 --> 00:08:47,756
Try it. It'll bring out your empathy.

150
00:08:56,098 --> 00:08:57,141
It's good.

151
00:08:57,224 --> 00:08:58,308
See, I told you.

152
00:09:05,649 --> 00:09:06,859
Hello, Mr. Yang.

153
00:09:07,151 --> 00:09:10,195
I just arrived at the store.

154
00:09:10,279 --> 00:09:12,072
Sure, I'll send you a photo.

155
00:09:12,156 --> 00:09:13,365
All right.

156
00:09:13,907 --> 00:09:15,868
VITAMIN ENERGY DRINK

157
00:09:25,335 --> 00:09:27,713
Hello, sir.
Thank you for your hard work.

158
00:09:27,796 --> 00:09:29,256
Hey, get off me.

159
00:09:29,339 --> 00:09:30,632
I'm already hot as it is.

160
00:09:31,550 --> 00:09:32,885
My goodness.

161
00:09:32,968 --> 00:09:34,887
Construction is practically done.

162
00:09:34,970 --> 00:09:35,971
Done, my foot.

163
00:09:36,054 --> 00:09:37,431
We've got a long way to go.

164
00:09:37,514 --> 00:09:39,558
We worked until 2 a.m. last night.

165
00:09:40,184 --> 00:09:42,561
Don't give us last-minute orders.

166
00:09:42,644 --> 00:09:44,354
You always cut it close.

167
00:09:46,106 --> 00:09:47,733
Come on now.

168
00:09:48,400 --> 00:09:50,277
Have a drink, sir.

169
00:09:50,360 --> 00:09:51,361
- Fine.
- All right.

170
00:09:53,155 --> 00:09:54,781
Have a drink while you work.

171
00:09:56,200 --> 00:09:58,035
Here you go.
Thank you for your hard work.

172
00:10:00,329 --> 00:10:02,998
Gosh, it's so dusty in here.

173
00:10:03,665 --> 00:10:05,083
This just won't do.

174
00:10:06,877 --> 00:10:08,503
Hi, is this General Affairs?

175
00:10:08,587 --> 00:10:10,297
I'm calling from the Laknes store.

176
00:10:10,380 --> 00:10:12,007
Can you send someone to vacuum?

177
00:10:12,674 --> 00:10:13,675
Sorry?

178
00:10:13,759 --> 00:10:17,304
You should know
where the Laknes store is by now.

179
00:10:17,930 --> 00:10:21,391
Do you have any idea
how hard these people are working?

180
00:10:22,142 --> 00:10:24,394
Yes, please be more considerate.

181
00:10:24,770 --> 00:10:26,855
Thank you in advance.

182
00:10:27,898 --> 00:10:29,441
- Jeez.
- Goodness.

183
00:10:29,524 --> 00:10:31,443
You Hongsung people, I swear...

184
00:10:31,902 --> 00:10:34,363
So should we start
the electrical work?

185
00:10:35,072 --> 00:10:36,073
You're the best.

186
00:10:36,657 --> 00:10:38,450
We're counting on you.

187
00:10:38,533 --> 00:10:39,534
Whatever.

188
00:10:40,410 --> 00:10:41,954
Let's start on electrical.

189
00:10:42,037 --> 00:10:43,163
We can follow the blueprint.

190
00:10:43,247 --> 00:10:44,957
All right, let's see.

191
00:10:45,249 --> 00:10:47,125
Since this is a clothing store...

192
00:10:47,209 --> 00:10:50,212
- These aren't heavy at all.
- Just leave them. We'll handle it.

193
00:10:50,295 --> 00:10:52,130
It's the least I can do.

194
00:10:52,506 --> 00:10:53,590
Light as a feather.

195
00:11:15,862 --> 00:11:18,031
- Hey, Gi-tae.
<i>- Hello, Mr. Yang.</i>

196
00:11:18,115 --> 00:11:19,658
<i>Construction is going well.</i>

197
00:11:19,741 --> 00:11:21,201
They're cleaning up now.

198
00:11:21,285 --> 00:11:23,495
<i>Okay, good work.</i>
<i>Are you coming back now?</i>

199
00:11:23,578 --> 00:11:25,998
Oh, since I'm here

200
00:11:26,081 --> 00:11:28,583
I figured I'd make my rounds
at the other stores.

201
00:11:28,667 --> 00:11:31,003
Good idea. But don't go empty-handed.

202
00:11:31,086 --> 00:11:32,754
<i>Buy them something to drink.</i>

203
00:11:32,838 --> 00:11:34,840
Understood, sir.

204
00:11:34,923 --> 00:11:37,009
I'll see you later, then.

205
00:11:37,092 --> 00:11:38,510
All right. Good work.

206
00:11:41,096 --> 00:11:42,806
Gi-tae's gotten pretty savvy.

207
00:11:44,016 --> 00:11:46,310
- It looks too cramped, doesn't it?
- Yes.

208
00:11:46,810 --> 00:11:48,270
It might fall off the edge.

209
00:11:49,438 --> 00:11:51,815
How about this...

210
00:11:53,066 --> 00:11:54,192
I think it's okay now.

211
00:11:59,323 --> 00:12:01,074
Over here, Mr. Jeong.

212
00:12:07,497 --> 00:12:09,207
Were you checking on construction?

213
00:12:10,542 --> 00:12:11,543
Yes.

214
00:12:20,969 --> 00:12:21,970
Have a seat.

215
00:12:32,356 --> 00:12:34,024
Did you make your rounds?

216
00:12:34,399 --> 00:12:37,486
Yes, I said hello
to everyone at the office.

217
00:12:37,778 --> 00:12:39,404
How does it feel to be back?

218
00:12:41,031 --> 00:12:42,366
It's great, of course.

219
00:12:43,033 --> 00:12:44,368
A bit awkward too.

220
00:12:45,744 --> 00:12:46,995
You must have a lot on your mind.

221
00:12:48,497 --> 00:12:50,374
I'm not entirely at ease.

222
00:12:52,125 --> 00:12:53,877
It wasn't an easy decision
for me, either.

223
00:12:54,920 --> 00:12:57,631
I wasn't sure taking you in
was the right call.

224
00:12:59,841 --> 00:13:02,302
I completely understand
where you're coming from.

225
00:13:02,386 --> 00:13:03,720
Let me be clear.

226
00:13:04,179 --> 00:13:06,556
Just because I approved it
doesn't mean I was happy about it.

227
00:13:07,974 --> 00:13:09,017
Yes, ma'am.

228
00:13:10,310 --> 00:13:13,146
The audit of the China branch
is starting now.

229
00:13:13,230 --> 00:13:16,274
Depending on the outcome,
it could turn into a criminal case.

230
00:13:16,358 --> 00:13:17,401
Are you aware of that?

231
00:13:17,901 --> 00:13:19,444
Yes, I'm aware.

232
00:13:19,528 --> 00:13:21,279
I can't help but wonder.

233
00:13:21,363 --> 00:13:23,990
All personnel transfers were frozen

234
00:13:24,616 --> 00:13:27,035
but how did just one person
transfer to Korea?

235
00:13:27,577 --> 00:13:28,578
On top of that

236
00:13:29,621 --> 00:13:32,040
I heard a complaint
was filed against you.

237
00:13:33,708 --> 00:13:36,628
Did you abandon a sinking ship
to save yourself?

238
00:13:42,008 --> 00:13:44,344
I don't know
if you can't say anything

239
00:13:44,428 --> 00:13:46,763
or if you're just choosing
to stay silent.

240
00:13:49,057 --> 00:13:50,475
But I think it's possible

241
00:13:50,559 --> 00:13:53,979
you're in league with the people
who embezzled from the China branch.

242
00:13:54,062 --> 00:13:55,063
But...

243
00:13:55,647 --> 00:13:58,316
We shouldn't assume anything
without evidence.

244
00:13:59,484 --> 00:14:01,027
That's why I took you in.

245
00:14:02,654 --> 00:14:03,655
Yes, ma'am.

246
00:14:04,614 --> 00:14:06,783
There's only one thing
you can do here.

247
00:14:08,952 --> 00:14:10,495
Work hard.

248
00:14:11,705 --> 00:14:15,459
If the audit results are positive,
that's great news for you.

249
00:14:16,001 --> 00:14:17,669
And even if they're negative

250
00:14:18,170 --> 00:14:21,381
your hard work will still count
for something.

251
00:14:22,007 --> 00:14:23,467
Do you get what I'm saying?

252
00:14:24,134 --> 00:14:25,135
Yes, ma'am.

253
00:14:25,802 --> 00:14:27,596
All right, you may go.

254
00:14:29,890 --> 00:14:30,891
Yes, ma'am.

255
00:15:05,675 --> 00:15:08,845
2 MONTHS AGO, CHINA

256
00:15:10,764 --> 00:15:11,765
POINT OF CONTACT

257
00:15:11,848 --> 00:15:13,350
TRADING COMPANY TRANSACTIONS

258
00:15:27,030 --> 00:15:28,532
COPY TO USB DRIVE

259
