Fine, let's say
they went out of business.

332
00:21:27,265 --> 00:21:29,142
They already failed once.

333
00:21:29,225 --> 00:21:31,352
Would they try again without a plan?

334
00:21:31,436 --> 00:21:34,689
They prepared thoroughly
for their comeback.

335
00:21:35,273 --> 00:21:38,192
Being prepared is great and all

336
00:21:38,276 --> 00:21:40,486
but Ms. Cha recently...

337
00:21:42,363 --> 00:21:43,865
Can I tell them?

338
00:21:44,115 --> 00:21:45,867
Of course not.

339
00:21:45,950 --> 00:21:47,493
- I shouldn't.
- What is it?

340
00:21:47,827 --> 00:21:49,245
So the thing is

341
00:21:49,704 --> 00:21:51,039
she got an offer from a certain brand

342
00:21:51,122 --> 00:21:54,250
to run their flagship store
in Seongsu-dong.

343
00:21:55,877 --> 00:21:56,961
Habsburg?

344
00:21:57,587 --> 00:21:59,464
How did you...

345
00:21:59,547 --> 00:22:01,799
Of course, I know everything
that happens in this industry.

346
00:22:02,884 --> 00:22:04,052
But that place is...

347
00:22:04,677 --> 00:22:06,095
Sure, it's nice.

348
00:22:06,179 --> 00:22:07,931
We can't stop you from going there.

349
00:22:08,473 --> 00:22:11,851
Don't they offer managers
a 15% commission?

350
00:22:11,935 --> 00:22:14,062
I'm sure that's true
for the first month.

351
00:22:14,145 --> 00:22:16,648
But they'll lower it
after their opening month.

352
00:22:16,731 --> 00:22:17,774
I already know.

353
00:22:19,192 --> 00:22:20,276
How do you know?

354
00:22:21,694 --> 00:22:24,072
Those punks always
pull the same scheme.

355
00:22:24,155 --> 00:22:25,156
Ms. Cha.

356
00:22:25,448 --> 00:22:27,241
I wasn't going to say this, but...

357
00:22:31,287 --> 00:22:32,288
Sis.

358
00:22:32,372 --> 00:22:34,499
You're really breaking my heart.

359
00:22:34,874 --> 00:22:35,875
What?

360
00:22:36,960 --> 00:22:38,169
Why are you so naive?

361
00:22:39,045 --> 00:22:41,422
You've been played so many times,
but you still don't get it.

362
00:22:41,506 --> 00:22:43,424
This isn't the first time
they've pulled this.

363
00:22:44,050 --> 00:22:46,636
Why do you keep working with them
when they play you every time?

364
00:22:46,719 --> 00:22:49,138
Why do you always turn us down

365
00:22:49,222 --> 00:22:51,766
and choose to suffer
working with those punks?

366
00:22:51,849 --> 00:22:55,269
I swear I'm not saying this
because you won't work with us.

367
00:22:55,937 --> 00:22:58,356
How many years
have we known each other?

368
00:22:58,439 --> 00:23:01,484
It just breaks my heart
to see you go through that!

369
00:23:01,567 --> 00:23:03,528
Maybe you should stop drinking,
Mr. Yang.

370
00:23:04,195 --> 00:23:06,489
Imagine she were your sister!

371
00:23:07,991 --> 00:23:08,992
Sis.

372
00:23:09,659 --> 00:23:10,743
Just promise me one thing.

373
00:23:12,120 --> 00:23:14,288
I can't force you to work with us

374
00:23:14,706 --> 00:23:17,542
but just don't let them hurt you.

375
00:23:17,959 --> 00:23:20,128
Give it your best shot.

376
00:23:20,795 --> 00:23:22,130
That's all I ask.

377
00:23:26,592 --> 00:23:28,428
Damn, you almost got me.

378
00:23:28,761 --> 00:23:30,555
That was so close.

379
00:23:30,638 --> 00:23:32,015
I thought you were actually drunk.

380
00:23:32,098 --> 00:23:34,058
- We've got a long way to go.
- Oh, my gosh.

381
00:23:34,142 --> 00:23:35,518
- The night is young.
- Jeez.

382
00:23:36,102 --> 00:23:37,478
- Cheers.
- Cheers.

383
00:23:38,980 --> 00:23:40,815
<i>She's so smart</i>

384
00:23:40,898 --> 00:23:42,608
<i>She's so charming</i>

385
00:23:42,692 --> 00:23:45,153
<i>She drives me crazy</i>
<i>I like her so much...</i>

386
00:23:45,236 --> 00:23:46,696
Goodness.

387
00:23:47,071 --> 00:23:48,197
Your glass is empty.

388
00:23:48,281 --> 00:23:49,741
Let me pour you a drink.

389
00:23:50,658 --> 00:23:54,078
I keep drinking,
but I wonder if it's poisoned.

390
00:23:54,162 --> 00:23:56,372
No poison, just sincerity.

391
00:23:56,456 --> 00:23:57,582
Pour me one too.

392
00:23:57,915 --> 00:24:00,376
I can't deal with you, Mr. Yang.

393
00:24:00,460 --> 00:24:01,836
That's too bad. Deal with it.

394
00:24:02,628 --> 00:24:06,132
When we get the Laknes samples,
I'll save you a horsehair bag.

395
00:24:06,966 --> 00:24:09,135
If you're giving me one,
make it alligator.

396
00:24:09,844 --> 00:24:12,221
Alligator is nice too

397
00:24:12,305 --> 00:24:14,223
but you haven't seen
their burgundy horsehair.

398
00:24:14,307 --> 00:24:15,475
It's beautiful.

399
00:24:15,558 --> 00:24:17,185
Horsehair or alligator,
it doesn't matter.

400
00:24:17,268 --> 00:24:18,895
The timing couldn't be worse.

401
00:24:18,978 --> 00:24:20,229
Why did it have to be now?

402
00:24:24,150 --> 00:24:25,193
Do you think it'll work?

403
00:24:28,112 --> 00:24:29,113
I don't know.

404
00:24:29,489 --> 00:24:32,700
Goodness, how can you say that
when you came here to convince me?

405
00:24:33,785 --> 00:24:35,953
I'll be honest with you, Ms. Cha.

406
00:24:36,037 --> 00:24:37,580
I'm not sure about Laknes.

407
00:24:37,830 --> 00:24:40,708
But with you,
I think we can make it work.

408
00:24:41,250 --> 00:24:43,252
Well, aren't you a smooth talker?

409
00:24:43,628 --> 00:24:45,254
Even if it's the same brand

410
00:24:45,338 --> 00:24:48,800
there can be a huge gap in revenue
depending on the manager.

411
00:24:48,883 --> 00:24:50,051
You know that yourself.

412
00:24:50,426 --> 00:24:53,221
I wouldn't ask you
if I didn't believe in this brand.

413
00:24:53,638 --> 00:24:55,848
If anyone could sell it,
then I'd ask anyone.

414
00:24:56,766 --> 00:24:58,935
But this is something
only you can do.

415
00:24:59,852 --> 00:25:02,563
Is that a good thing or a bad thing?

416
00:25:02,647 --> 00:25:04,440
As for incentives and benefits

417
00:25:04,524 --> 00:25:06,818
I'll match the highest
industry standards.

418
00:25:07,276 --> 00:25:09,112
Let's give it a shot, Ms. Cha.

419
00:25:11,197 --> 00:25:12,657
I'm getting played again.

420
00:25:13,407 --> 00:25:14,450
Come on.

421
00:25:14,534 --> 00:25:15,827
Have a drink.

422
00:25:16,953 --> 00:25:17,954
Drink up.

423
00:25:22,458 --> 00:25:26,504
<i>I know you really need me</i>

424
00:25:26,587 --> 00:25:28,506
<i>- You're too perfect</i>
<i>- You're too perfect</i>

425
00:25:28,589 --> 00:25:29,799
<i>- I saw your eyes...</i>
<i>- I saw your eyes...</i>

426
00:25:29,882 --> 00:25:32,844
SINCHON <i>SEOLLEONGTANG</i>

427
00:25:41,644 --> 00:25:43,980
Jeez, those chicks can really drink.

428
00:25:45,064 --> 00:25:46,983
Why say that
after you had such a good time?

429
00:25:47,817 --> 00:25:48,818
Sorry?

430
00:25:50,611 --> 00:25:51,946
It's not right

431
00:25:52,029 --> 00:25:54,490
to bad-mouth people
after having a good time with them.

432
00:25:54,574 --> 00:25:56,367
We're the ones who need them.

433
00:25:57,243 --> 00:25:58,327
Well...

434
00:25:58,411 --> 00:26:00,746
I wasn't exactly bad-mouthing them.

435
00:26:00,830 --> 00:26:04,167
It was more like
an expression of surprise.

436
00:26:04,250 --> 00:26:06,752
Then just say
they can really hold their liquor.

437
00:26:06,836 --> 00:26:09,172
Why are you calling them chicks
and saying they drink too much?

438
00:26:10,590 --> 00:26:12,967
You've been sprouting up lately.

439
00:26:13,050 --> 00:26:14,260
Should I nip that in the bud?

440
00:26:15,553 --> 00:26:16,596
I'm sorry, sir.

441
00:26:18,639 --> 00:26:20,141
- Mr. Yang.
- Thank you.

442
00:26:22,476 --> 00:26:24,061
- Gi-tae.
- Yes, sir.

443
00:26:25,021 --> 00:26:26,355
It's not just you, Gi-tae.

444
00:26:26,439 --> 00:26:27,481
That's human nature.

445
00:26:27,940 --> 00:26:29,567
Everyone's different
behind closed doors.

446
00:26:29,984 --> 00:26:31,235
It's best to be careful.

447
00:26:32,528 --> 00:26:34,113
Yes, sir. I'll keep that in mind.

448
00:26:36,032 --> 00:26:38,826
Don't forget what I said,
even if you go to a new company.

449
00:26:39,660 --> 00:26:40,661
Yes, sir.

450
00:26:41,996 --> 00:26:42,997
Sorry?

451
00:26:43,414 --> 00:26:46,125
So have you made a decision?

452
00:26:46,209 --> 00:26:47,376
Are you leaving the company?

453
00:26:47,835 --> 00:26:48,836
What?

454
00:26:49,086 --> 00:26:50,213
Are you quitting, Park Gi-tae?

455
00:26:51,297 --> 00:26:53,007
What? I mean...

456
00:26:53,549 --> 00:26:54,884
What's with that guilty look?

457
00:26:54,967 --> 00:26:56,219
You did nothing wrong.

458
00:26:56,302 --> 00:26:57,678
I'm just curious.

459
00:26:57,762 --> 00:27:01,182
<i>The luck that passed me by</i>
<i>came together...</i>

460
00:27:01,265 --> 00:27:03,100
- Gi-tae, increase the echo.
- Okay.

461
00:27:03,184 --> 00:27:09,106
<i>It became you and came to me</i>

462
00:27:09,190 --> 00:27:13,194
<i>In a rainstorm</i>

463
00:27:13,486 --> 00:27:14,528
<i>I'll become...</i>

464
00:27:14,612 --> 00:27:16,822
Thank you for the offer, Mr. Gong.

465
00:27:17,323 --> 00:27:19,075
Thank you for seeing me.

466
00:27:19,158 --> 00:27:21,702
But why did you come yourself
this time?

467
00:27:21,786 --> 00:27:24,038
Mr. Yang was always the one
who went drinking with us.

468
00:27:24,413 --> 00:27:27,250
I thought you weren't on good terms
with your team.

469
00:27:27,667 --> 00:27:29,460
I can't say that's entirely false.

470
00:27:30,044 --> 00:27:31,045
Are things better now?

471
00:27:31,671 --> 00:27:34,757
<i>...I'll go anywhere</i>

472
00:27:34,840 --> 00:27:36,842
<i>Trust in me now...</i>

473
00:27:36,926 --> 00:27:39,220
Yes, I'm working on it.

474
00:27:41,847 --> 00:27:44,892
You should work a little harder.

475
00:27:46,102 --> 00:27:47,103
Pardon?

476
00:27:50,314 --> 00:27:53,359
<i>You know Mr. Jeong</i>
<i>started his own business.</i>

477
00:27:55,111 --> 00:27:57,530
<i>Did you know</i>
<i>he's been trying to scout people?</i>

478
00:27:57,905 --> 00:27:59,573
He's much more friendly now.

479
00:28:00,157 --> 00:28:01,325
Really? Mr. Gong?

480
00:28:01,409 --> 00:28:02,576
- Yes.
- No way.

481
00:28:05,538 --> 00:28:08,916
<i>Trust in me now</i>

482
00:28:11,377 --> 00:28:13,254
- Let's go, Laknes!
- Let's go!

483
00:28:14,130 --> 00:28:16,507
I wasn't trying to hide it from you.

484
00:28:16,966 --> 00:28:19,593
But I did get an offer
from Mr. Jeong.

485
00:28:20,136 --> 00:28:23,556
Hey, you should've told us
right away.

486
00:28:24,390 --> 00:28:25,391
I'm sorry, it's just...

487
00:28:26,100 --> 00:28:28,686
I didn't know how to bring it up.

488
00:28:28,769 --> 00:28:29,770
So the thing is...

489
00:28:30,896 --> 00:28:32,148
How do I say this?

490
00:28:32,398 --> 00:28:33,816
I'm not the only one

491
00:28:34,984 --> 00:28:37,069
Mr. Jeong made an offer to.

492
00:28:38,821 --> 00:28:40,323
What are you saying?

493
00:28:41,741 --> 00:28:47,038
He made offers to employees
on other teams as well.

494
00:28:47,538 --> 00:28:48,831
That seemed a bit problematic.

495
00:28:49,332 --> 00:28:51,584
So I was trying to think
of a way to tell you.

496
00:28:53,461 --> 00:28:54,587
As far as I know...

497
00:28:56,255 --> 00:28:57,423
It's more than four people.

498
00:29:00,092 --> 00:29:03,137
What exactly is he trying to do?

499
00:29:06,432 --> 00:29:07,808
<i>What did Ms. Park say?</i>

500
00:29:08,309 --> 00:29:09,769
What do you think?

501
00:29:09,852 --> 00:29:11,896
I said I was quitting,
and she said okay.

502
00:29:13,105 --> 00:29:15,149
Maybe she thought it was inevitable.

503
00:29:15,232 --> 00:29:16,817
She might've even felt grateful.

504
00:29:17,318 --> 00:29:18,319
Hey.

505
00:29:18,527 --> 00:29:19,862
I have to move aside

506
00:29:19,945 --> 00:29:22,073
so people like you
can move up the ladder.

507
00:29:24,742 --> 00:29:27,161
If you resign, where will you go?

508
00:29:30,289 --> 00:29:32,833
You're going to quit at 40
without a plan?

509
00:29:33,542 --> 00:29:35,044
Does your wife know?

510
00:29:35,127 --> 00:29:36,629
Of course, she does.

511
00:29:36,712 --> 00:29:37,963
She told me to do whatever I want.

512
00:29:38,547 --> 00:29:40,674
But she said she'd kill me
if I can't support the family.

513
00:29:48,766 --> 00:29:49,934
Don't you have regrets?

514
00:29:50,309 --> 00:29:51,477
Yes, I do.

515
00:29:53,104 --> 00:29:55,314
Sometimes, I wonder
if I should've worked harder.

516
00:29:55,398 --> 00:29:56,524
If I had

517
00:29:57,233 --> 00:29:59,360
could I have been
a candidate for associate director?

518
00:29:59,443 --> 00:30:00,444
That sort of thing.

519
00:30:01,153 --> 00:30:02,154
Mr. Jeong.

520
00:30:03,364 --> 00:30:05,699
If you just get through
this promotion cycle

521
00:30:05,783 --> 00:30:07,201
I think you'll have a shot.

522
00:30:08,202 --> 00:30:09,203
Hey.

523
00:30:09,620 --> 00:30:11,330
You're skilled

524
00:30:11,414 --> 00:30:14,166
and gaining good work experience,
so you might not know this.

525
00:30:14,542 --> 00:30:17,002
But I wasn't promoted to team leader
based on my skills.

526
00:30:17,086 --> 00:30:18,254
It was based on seniority.

527
00:30:19,380 --> 00:30:22,591
Do you know the highest position
you can reach through seniority?

528
00:30:23,717 --> 00:30:25,010
Team leader.

529
00:30:25,094 --> 00:30:26,220
I'm a team leader.

530
00:30:26,595 --> 00:30:27,596
It's over for me.

531
00:30:30,141 --> 00:30:32,017
Aren't you thinking too negatively?

532
00:30:32,101 --> 00:30:33,727
You're the best at this job.

533
00:30:33,811 --> 00:30:35,020
What are you talking about?

534
00:30:35,938 --> 00:30:37,022
Thanks for saying that.

535
00:30:37,106 --> 00:30:38,107
Jeez.

536
00:30:42,486 --> 00:30:43,487
Eun-tae.

537
00:30:44,321 --> 00:30:45,364
Someday

538
00:30:46,240 --> 00:30:49,326
if we ever meet again through work

539
00:30:50,494 --> 00:30:52,163
I hope you won't be
too disappointed in me.

540
00:30:53,330 --> 00:30:54,748
What are you saying?

541
00:30:54,832 --> 00:30:56,000
I'm just saying.

542
00:30:56,083 --> 00:30:57,626
I hope you don't feel that way.

543
00:31:16,395 --> 00:31:18,439
INCOMING CALL
TEAM 4 MR. JEONG SEON-HYUK

544
00:31:22,026 --> 00:31:25,404
ASSISTANT MANAGER GONG EUN-TAE

545
00:31:25,488 --> 00:31:26,864
<i>- Hello?</i>
- Hey, Eun-tae.

546
00:31:27,114 --> 00:31:28,199
Did you eat dinner?

547
00:31:28,616 --> 00:31:29,950
<i>Why are you doing this?</i>

548
00:31:30,951 --> 00:31:32,286
What are you referring to?

549
00:31:32,786 --> 00:31:35,080
Not showing up to work
after resigning

550
00:31:35,331 --> 00:31:37,124
<i>or poaching employees?</i>

551
00:31:37,541 --> 00:31:38,542
Both, I suppose.

552
00:31:41,295 --> 00:31:43,130
<i>Well, once I thought about it</i>

553
00:31:43,631 --> 00:31:45,716
I realized I couldn't fake a smile
and say goodbye

554
00:31:45,799 --> 00:31:47,927
when I'm betraying everyone.

555
00:31:48,719 --> 00:31:50,346
That's why I haven't been to work.

556
00:31:51,013 --> 00:31:52,890
And it's true that I made job offers.

557
00:31:53,390 --> 00:31:54,934
<i>They can make their own decisions.</i>

558
00:31:55,017 --> 00:31:57,603
So did you just call me
to ask if I had dinner?

559
00:31:59,939 --> 00:32:02,233
So what is Hongsung going to do?

560
00:32:03,734 --> 00:32:05,736
They'll have to punish me somehow.

561
00:32:06,987 --> 00:32:08,531
What exactly are you expecting?

562
00:32:09,240 --> 00:32:11,325
I'm sure you're not far off.

563
00:32:12,034 --> 00:32:13,160
Is that right?

564
00:32:14,370 --> 00:32:15,454
What about you?

565
00:32:16,121 --> 00:32:17,289
Will you stay at Hongsung?

566
00:32:22,044 --> 00:32:23,879
- What do you mean?
<i>- Do you know</i>

567
00:32:24,588 --> 00:32:27,007
what they all say
when I offer them a job?

568
00:32:27,800 --> 00:32:29,718
They thank me
for recognizing their worth.

569
00:32:30,302 --> 00:32:32,721
Hongsung doesn't know
how to develop its employees.

570
00:32:33,097 --> 00:32:35,015
<i>I mean, they have a guy like you</i>

571
00:32:35,099 --> 00:32:37,726
<i>caught up in office politics</i>
<i>and doing odd jobs.</i>

572
00:32:38,185 --> 00:32:41,230
So why don't you take this chance
to think about it?

573
00:32:43,190 --> 00:32:44,692
<i>I'll pretend we never had</i>
<i>this conversation.</i>

574
00:32:48,362 --> 00:32:50,573
HONGSUNG SALES DIVISION 1
TEAM LEADER JEONG SEON-HYUK

575
00:32:50,656 --> 00:32:51,657
Eun-tae.

576
00:32:52,783 --> 00:32:54,618
You're the reason I'm leaving.

577
00:32:55,452 --> 00:32:57,246
<i>I made this decision because of you.</i>

578
00:33:00,874 --> 00:33:06,130
<i>All I did was find the courage</i>
<i>to do the job I'd been given.</i>

579
00:33:07,464 --> 00:33:12,595
<i>I had no idea that courage</i>
<i>would lead to this result.</i>

580
00:33:13,095 --> 00:33:14,179
You see...

581
00:33:15,556 --> 00:33:16,807
I think...

582
00:33:19,560 --> 00:33:21,270
I'll become Hongsung's enemy.

583
00:33:22,688 --> 00:33:25,399
<i>You could say the one</i>
<i>who made him Hongsung's enemy...</i>

584
00:33:27,568 --> 00:33:28,902
<i>was me.</i>

585
00:33:38,621 --> 00:33:40,372
- Good morning.
- Hello, Mr. Gong.

586
00:33:41,206 --> 00:33:43,042
- Hello.
- Hello.

587
00:33:43,709 --> 00:33:45,544
- Hello.
- Hello, sir.

588
00:33:46,045 --> 00:33:47,129
Hello.

589
00:33:47,212 --> 00:33:49,632
- You're here early, Ms. Jang.
- Hello, Mr. Gong.

590
00:33:49,715 --> 00:33:51,216
Good morning, Mr. Gong.

591
00:34:01,393 --> 00:34:04,146
What's going on between you two?

592
00:34:04,563 --> 00:34:05,564
Look at this.

593
00:34:09,151 --> 00:34:10,527
Didn't she do a great job?

594
00:34:10,611 --> 00:34:12,404
Ji-hye worked very hard on it.

595
00:34:13,030 --> 00:34:15,366
You didn't stay up all night
for this, did you?

596
00:34:16,867 --> 00:34:17,868
Please tell me you didn't.

597
00:34:19,495 --> 00:34:20,496
I'm sorry, Ms. Jang.

598
00:34:20,996 --> 00:34:24,333
Tell me if anything is missing
or needs to be revised.

599
00:34:24,416 --> 00:34:25,793
I'll fix it right away.

600
00:34:26,585 --> 00:34:28,087
What I'm trying to say is...

601
00:34:33,217 --> 00:34:34,468
Ji-hye.

602
00:34:35,135 --> 00:34:36,887
Do you have the original file?

603
00:34:37,221 --> 00:34:40,140
Yes, I shared it
on the company network.

604
00:34:40,516 --> 00:34:41,600
That's great.

605
00:34:41,684 --> 00:34:44,144
Let's use it as our team's manual.

606
00:34:45,020 --> 00:34:46,021
Sorry?

607
00:34:47,189 --> 00:34:48,732
I'm really sorry, Ji-hye.

608
00:34:48,816 --> 00:34:50,359
I should have been clearer.

609
00:34:51,276 --> 00:34:54,113
I was just asking
for a simple document

610
00:34:54,196 --> 00:34:56,281
so I could begin working right away.

611
00:34:56,365 --> 00:34:58,492
I wasn't asking you
to write a full report.

612
00:34:59,785 --> 00:35:01,245
It's not like I'm a director.

613
00:35:01,328 --> 00:35:03,288
I mean, this is flawless.

614
00:35:04,331 --> 00:35:06,125
Even I can't make
something like this.

615
00:35:09,169 --> 00:35:13,215
I was going to tell her,
but she was doing such a good job.

616
00:35:13,298 --> 00:35:14,883
I wanted to see the final result...

617
00:35:17,803 --> 00:35:18,804
Ji-hye?

618
00:35:22,891 --> 00:35:23,976
I'm sorry.

619
00:35:25,269 --> 00:35:27,104
I don't know what's wrong with me.

620
00:35:30,190 --> 00:35:31,442
I'm sorry.

621
00:35:37,906 --> 00:35:39,533
I bet you've never been up here.

622
00:35:40,159 --> 00:35:41,201
No, I haven't.

623
00:35:42,327 --> 00:35:44,705
I didn't even know
we had a place like this.

624
00:35:46,832 --> 00:35:47,833
I'm sorry.

625
00:35:48,584 --> 00:35:50,586
I'm sorry
I didn't bring you here sooner

626
00:35:50,669 --> 00:35:52,963
especially after you've been here
for over four months.

627
00:35:54,047 --> 00:35:57,426
And as your team leader,
I didn't know how anxious you were.

628
00:35:57,509 --> 00:35:58,719
I'm also sorry for that.

629
00:35:59,470 --> 00:36:02,931
I loved seeing how hard you worked,
so I left you alone.

630
00:36:04,016 --> 00:36:05,601
I had no clue it was out of anxiety.

631
00:36:08,353 --> 00:36:10,814
You're a contract worker
who has just one year

632
00:36:10,898 --> 00:36:13,025
to prove yourself
if you want to stay here.

633
00:36:13,108 --> 00:36:14,359
It must be tough.

634
00:36:15,277 --> 00:36:17,529
Well, I'm not the only one
in that position.

635
00:36:18,822 --> 00:36:20,365
I can do a better job.

636
00:36:21,784 --> 00:36:23,243
What exactly can you do better,
and how?

637
00:36:24,495 --> 00:36:25,496
I'll be honest.

638
00:36:26,955 --> 00:36:28,248
I can't tell you

639
00:36:29,750 --> 00:36:32,419
to trust me and follow my lead,
or that hard work is all you need.

640
00:36:33,837 --> 00:36:34,963
But instead

641
00:36:35,380 --> 00:36:37,633
I'll do everything I can
to deliver results

642
00:36:37,716 --> 00:36:39,718
starting with Laknes.

643
00:36:40,594 --> 00:36:43,222
If the team gets good results,
I'll gain leverage as team leader.

644
00:36:43,597 --> 00:36:46,266
Then I'll have the confidence
to advocate for you

645
00:36:46,350 --> 00:36:51,480
because Sales Team 5 needs you,
no matter what.

646
00:37:02,366 --> 00:37:03,700
What is this?

647
00:37:04,326 --> 00:37:05,869
It's the file you worked on.

648
00:37:06,537 --> 00:37:07,538
Keep it in your wallet.

649
00:37:08,580 --> 00:37:09,998
Regardless of the outcome

650
00:37:11,166 --> 00:37:14,878
it doesn't change your worth
as the person who made this.

651
00:37:16,296 --> 00:37:18,090
Don't put your faith in the company.

652
00:37:18,799 --> 00:37:20,133
Don't put your faith in me, either.

653
00:37:20,551 --> 00:37:23,679
Trust in your own worth
as the creator of that file.

654
00:37:28,433 --> 00:37:30,435
Thank you, Mr. Gong.

655
00:37:34,064 --> 00:37:35,315
Stay up here a little longer.

656
00:37:35,858 --> 00:37:37,401
Just don't stay here all day.

657
00:37:41,738 --> 00:37:42,739
Mr. Gong.

658
00:37:43,949 --> 00:37:47,786
If I become a full-time employee,
I'll treat you to a meal.

659
00:37:49,162 --> 00:37:50,163
No.

660
00:37:51,582 --> 00:37:52,791
I'll treat you.

661
00:37:53,709 --> 00:37:55,669
I promise I'll buy you
something delicious!

662
00:37:56,253 --> 00:37:57,379
Make it premium Korean beef.

663
00:37:59,381 --> 00:38:00,382
All right.

664
00:38:19,651 --> 00:38:21,111
I'm sorry, Mr. Gong.

665
00:38:21,194 --> 00:38:22,529
I should've made
my instructions clearer.

666
00:38:23,739 --> 00:38:25,949
It was ultimately my mistake.

667
00:38:26,033 --> 00:38:27,117
Don't worry about it.

668
00:38:31,496 --> 00:38:32,497
Mr. Gong.

669
00:38:33,582 --> 00:38:35,709
I'm sure you have
many questions for me.

670
00:38:36,752 --> 00:38:38,086
Why haven't you asked me anything?

671
00:38:40,213 --> 00:38:42,049
If you had something to tell me,
you would've already.

672
00:38:43,133 --> 00:38:46,219
The fact that you haven't
means you're not ready yet.

673
00:38:48,889 --> 00:38:50,891
It wasn't an easy decision for me.

674
00:38:52,851 --> 00:38:54,853
Please just know that.

675
00:39:05,030 --> 00:39:06,365
<i>How many people in total?</i>

676
00:39:06,990 --> 00:39:08,867
Five, as far as we can tell.

677
00:39:08,951 --> 00:39:10,661
Team 1's Park Jin-u,
Team 2's Choi Ju-hui

678
00:39:10,744 --> 00:39:13,622
Team 3's Kang Yeong-seo,
Team 5's Park Gi-tae

679
00:39:14,331 --> 00:39:15,958
and Team 4's Oh Jeong-hyeon.

680
00:39:18,001 --> 00:39:19,753
He tried to completely
dismantle Team 4.

681
00:39:21,505 --> 00:39:22,756
- Mr. Oh.
- Yes, ma'am.

682
00:39:22,839 --> 00:39:23,966
I rejected him right away.

683
00:39:24,591 --> 00:39:26,468
Mr. Jeong didn't clock in
today, either?

684
00:39:27,344 --> 00:39:29,137
He also stopped taking our calls
since yesterday.

685
00:39:29,221 --> 00:39:30,222
I did some digging.

686
00:39:30,305 --> 00:39:33,392
He appears to be mainly importing
gray market products from Mantua.

687
00:39:33,725 --> 00:39:36,979
It seems he established contacts
in Mantua before he quit.

688
00:39:37,521 --> 00:39:40,482
He's also already taken
Safilo and Philipp Plein...

689
00:39:43,485 --> 00:39:44,486
Were you aware?

690
00:39:45,737 --> 00:39:47,489
Their sales figures were poor.

691
00:39:48,240 --> 00:39:50,659
It's been a while since they were
mentioned at the meetings.

692
00:39:53,704 --> 00:39:55,414
Why didn't you stop him?

693
00:39:56,456 --> 00:39:58,083
I figured I'd let him have that much.

694
00:39:58,750 --> 00:40:00,877
I couldn't promote him, anyway.

695
00:40:01,420 --> 00:40:03,171
And he needed to find his own path.

696
00:40:04,715 --> 00:40:06,633
But poaching our people is
taking it too far.

697
00:40:09,177 --> 00:40:10,929
- I think...
- Mr. Jang.

698
00:40:11,013 --> 00:40:12,014
Yes, ma'am.

699
00:40:12,764 --> 00:40:13,765
What are your thoughts?

700
00:40:22,357 --> 00:40:25,318
MULTI-BRAND SHOE STORE
PROJECT PROPOSAL

701
00:40:26,194 --> 00:40:27,279
What is this?

702
00:40:27,362 --> 00:40:29,239
A project proposal
for a multi-brand shoe store?

703
00:40:29,322 --> 00:40:33,118
What if we used this
to put some pressure on Mr. Jeong?

704
00:40:40,000 --> 00:40:41,001
Tell me.

705
00:40:42,419 --> 00:40:43,503
Do you want to take this on?

706
00:40:43,920 --> 00:40:45,130
I'd like the company to take it on.

707
00:40:45,797 --> 00:40:47,632
If you propose this
as associate director

708
00:40:47,716 --> 00:40:49,384
it won't just be Team 5's project.

709
00:40:49,468 --> 00:40:51,636
It'll become the entire
Sales Division's project.

710
00:41:00,479 --> 00:41:02,856
We have to break into this market
at some point, anyway.

711
00:41:03,565 --> 00:41:06,902
Even if we sue Mr. Jeong,
we won't gain anything.

712
00:41:07,277 --> 00:41:09,571
And filing a claim against
our Mantua partners will be useless.

713
00:41:09,654 --> 00:41:11,656
"We had no idea.
What do you expect us to do?"

714
00:41:11,740 --> 00:41:12,949
They'll feign ignorance.

715
00:41:13,700 --> 00:41:14,826
And, to be frank...

716
00:41:17,621 --> 00:41:20,332
we can't stop our employees
from wanting to leave.

717
00:41:21,083 --> 00:41:22,626
So I propose

718
00:41:22,876 --> 00:41:25,253
that we take all of Mantua back.

719
00:41:25,879 --> 00:41:29,591
You want to use the shoe supply
to put pressure on Mantua?

720
00:41:30,342 --> 00:41:32,803
Mr. Jeong gets his entire supply
from Mantua.

721
00:41:33,428 --> 00:41:37,599
So I suggest we become a client
Mantua can't afford to lose.

722
00:41:37,682 --> 00:41:39,184
So big that Mr. Jeong can't compete.

723
00:41:39,935 --> 00:41:41,394
We'll put in a supply order

724
00:41:42,854 --> 00:41:45,148
and cut off
Mr. Jeong's entire supply.

725
00:41:47,234 --> 00:41:48,443
Whose idea was this?

726
00:41:50,070 --> 00:41:51,446
It was Mr. Gong's.

727
00:41:57,327 --> 00:41:58,328
Mr. Gong.

728
00:41:59,496 --> 00:42:01,081
Why a multi-brand shoe store?

729
00:42:05,836 --> 00:42:08,088
With clothing or accessories

730
00:42:08,171 --> 00:42:11,967
we also have to worry about hangers,
displays, props, and more.

731
00:42:12,050 --> 00:42:14,344
The downside to shoes is
that the boxes are bulky.

732
00:42:14,427 --> 00:42:17,639
But they're easy to manage
and require less preparation.

733
00:42:17,722 --> 00:42:19,724
There's also less inventory per store

734
00:42:19,808 --> 00:42:21,268
and, after each season

735
00:42:21,351 --> 00:42:23,770
we can send leftovers to outlets,
which is an advantage.

736
00:42:24,938 --> 00:42:27,065
I believe it's a good project.

737
00:42:27,732 --> 00:42:29,568
Are you almost done
prepping the Laknes launch?

738
00:42:30,360 --> 00:42:31,361
Ms. Park.

739
00:42:32,529 --> 00:42:34,573
I came up with this project

740
00:42:35,157 --> 00:42:37,200
but it doesn't mean
only I can take it on.

741
00:42:37,784 --> 00:42:40,745
Even if you give it to another team,
I'll do my best to help out.

742
00:42:41,037 --> 00:42:42,038
Just answer the question.

743
00:42:43,915 --> 00:42:44,916
Yes.

744
00:42:45,500 --> 00:42:47,252
Construction of the store's interior
is complete.

745
00:42:47,794 --> 00:42:49,129
We've also recruited managers.

746
00:42:50,088 --> 00:42:51,339
So can you take this on?

747
00:42:52,048 --> 00:42:53,216
Yes, I can.

748
00:42:54,217 --> 00:42:55,677
- Mr. Jang.
- Yes, ma'am.

749
00:42:55,760 --> 00:42:57,220
Schedule a meeting
with the Finance Team.

750
00:42:57,637 --> 00:43:00,557
- Mr. Gong, resubmit your proposal.
- Yes, ma'am.

751
00:43:00,891 --> 00:43:03,143
- And get ready for a trip to Mantua.
- Okay.

752
00:43:04,311 --> 00:43:05,312
Goodbye, ma'am.

753
00:43:11,359 --> 00:43:12,360
Eun-tae.

754
00:43:13,695 --> 00:43:14,946
You should pace yourself.

755
00:43:15,280 --> 00:43:17,199
At this rate,
you'll leave the rest of us behind.

756
00:43:17,282 --> 00:43:19,868
He's right. If you're going to do
the multi-brand shoe store

757
00:43:19,951 --> 00:43:22,120
you should give us
some of your other brands.

758
00:43:23,205 --> 00:43:25,332
Okay, I'll discuss it with Mr. Jang.

759
00:43:25,415 --> 00:43:28,752
Yes, talk it over
and help Mr. Kim out.

760
00:43:29,628 --> 00:43:30,629
What?

761
00:43:31,004 --> 00:43:33,298
- What's that supposed to mean?
- Sorry?

762
00:43:33,381 --> 00:43:35,675
Who are you to tell him
to help me out?

763
00:43:36,426 --> 00:43:39,012
Why would I take anything
from a junior colleague?

764
00:43:39,095 --> 00:43:40,180
I mean...

765
00:43:40,680 --> 00:43:43,308
Weren't you planning on
taking some of his brands?

766
00:43:43,391 --> 00:43:44,768
Why are you pretending?

767
00:43:45,310 --> 00:43:46,394
Look at this bastard.

768
00:43:47,062 --> 00:43:48,271
Then what about you?

769
00:43:48,355 --> 00:43:50,232
Are you whining
because you couldn't even get scraps?

770
00:43:50,315 --> 00:43:51,650
"Whining"?

771
00:43:52,150 --> 00:43:53,193
Are you serious?

772
00:43:53,485 --> 00:43:56,947
You're the one
snooping around a junior's team

773
00:43:57,030 --> 00:43:58,448
looking for scraps to take.

774
00:43:58,865 --> 00:44:01,076
Has this bastard lost his mind?
Do you want to fight?

775
00:44:01,159 --> 00:44:03,286
Don't call me a bastard.
We're both team leaders.

776
00:44:03,370 --> 00:44:04,788
How dare you call me that?

777
00:44:04,871 --> 00:44:06,081
What are you, an associate director?

778
00:44:06,164 --> 00:44:07,165
Hey!

779
00:44:16,299 --> 00:44:18,385
What a great example you're setting
as team leaders.

780
00:44:19,427 --> 00:44:22,180
Why don't you get back to work
instead of fighting?

781
00:44:22,430 --> 00:44:23,890
Cut the nonsense.

782
00:44:48,498 --> 00:44:54,337
<i>At a company, one person's decision</i>
<i>inevitably affects others.</i>

783
00:44:57,048 --> 00:45:00,760
<i>Everyone here is</i>
<i>both a cause and an effect</i>

784
00:45:01,219 --> 00:45:02,220
<i>of one another.</i>

785
00:45:09,019 --> 00:45:13,940
THE ORDINARY JACKPOT

786
00:45:41,801 --> 00:45:44,929
2,034,320 WON SENT TO LEE JI-HYE
FROM HONGSUNG INTERNATIONAL

787
00:45:58,902 --> 00:46:00,070
Hello.

788
00:46:00,153 --> 00:46:01,196
Yes, hello.

789
00:46:01,488 --> 00:46:03,698
- How much is this?
- It's 32,000 won.

790
00:46:03,782 --> 00:46:05,116
Could you give me a discount?

791
00:46:05,200 --> 00:46:06,951
Hi, ladies.
Can I help you find something?

792
00:46:07,035 --> 00:46:08,036
- This is so pretty.
- This?

793
00:46:08,119 --> 00:46:09,204
If you like it...

794
00:46:17,128 --> 00:46:19,381
Excuse me, do you have that brown one
in another color?

795
00:46:20,090 --> 00:46:21,091
That's the last one we have.

796
00:46:22,092 --> 00:46:23,968
- How much is this?
- It's 60,000 won.

797
00:46:24,552 --> 00:46:25,887
All right, thank you.

798
00:46:31,226 --> 00:46:32,852
- Hello.
- Welcome.

799
00:46:32,936 --> 00:46:34,062
May I try this on?

800
00:46:35,063 --> 00:46:36,314
Thank you.

801
00:46:43,029 --> 00:46:44,114
Thank you.

802
00:46:44,614 --> 00:46:46,241
It looks great on you.

803
00:46:46,324 --> 00:46:47,492
- Do you think so?
- Yeah.

804
00:46:52,580 --> 00:46:54,707
- That one doesn't look good.
- Right?

805
00:46:57,919 --> 00:46:59,587
That one's so pretty on you.

806
00:46:59,671 --> 00:47:00,839
You should get it.

807
00:47:01,256 --> 00:47:02,340
Thank you.

808
00:47:02,424 --> 00:47:05,427
She said that when we first met.

809
00:47:05,510 --> 00:47:07,804
"Get me baseline margins
for the brands we're in charge of.

810
00:47:07,887 --> 00:47:09,973
Customer prices,
customer service manuals..."

811
00:47:10,306 --> 00:47:12,767
You have no idea, right?
But that's not all.

812
00:47:12,851 --> 00:47:15,270
Credit memo logs,
invoice checklists...

813
00:47:15,353 --> 00:47:17,605
She asked me to prepare all of that.

814
00:47:17,689 --> 00:47:19,732
But do you know what's really crazy?

815
00:47:19,816 --> 00:47:21,609
I memorized it all in one shot.

816
00:47:21,693 --> 00:47:24,237
Isn't it?
You know I'm bad at memorization.

817
00:47:24,320 --> 00:47:26,364
Remember when I ran into my ex
on the street

818
00:47:26,448 --> 00:47:28,700
and stuttered like crazy
because I forgot his name?

819
00:47:29,492 --> 00:47:31,077
I don't know. I still don't remember.

820
00:47:31,161 --> 00:47:33,371
But I memorized all of that
in one shot.

821
00:47:33,455 --> 00:47:34,706
Isn't that amazing?

822
00:47:35,623 --> 00:47:38,042
But you can't just memorize
the words.

823
00:47:38,126 --> 00:47:40,753
There's a logical sequence
based on the workflow.

824
00:47:40,837 --> 00:47:42,589
That's how I memorized it.

825
00:47:42,672 --> 00:47:45,133
Can you imagine how nervous I was?

826
00:47:45,425 --> 00:47:48,136
That assistant manager has
such a strong aura.

827
00:47:48,219 --> 00:47:50,680
She looks at you
like she's studying you.

828
00:47:51,723 --> 00:47:54,767
Like a customs officer
looking you over.

829
00:47:54,851 --> 00:47:56,728
So imagine how hard I worked.

830
00:47:56,811 --> 00:47:58,480
I even lost my appetite.

831
00:47:58,563 --> 00:48:01,274
So when I brought her the file,
do you know what she said...

832
00:48:02,192 --> 00:48:03,693
Yes, what is it?

833
00:48:04,527 --> 00:48:06,070
Your boyfriend came?

834
00:48:06,154 --> 00:48:07,989
Okay, let's talk later.

835
00:48:08,072 --> 00:48:09,115
Bye.

836
00:48:14,787 --> 00:48:16,915
But this is the highlight.

837
00:48:18,082 --> 00:48:20,126
She said I did a great job.

838
00:48:24,047 --> 00:48:25,173
Darn it.

839
00:48:29,969 --> 00:48:31,429
Whatever, I did great.

840
00:51:05,375 --> 00:51:07,377
Subtitles by Eunice Kim

